Computer Vision works upstream, estimates the world with many unknown parameters.
Many of the parameters are methods to estimate the world.

Many problems require data to learn.

Some of the virtual parameters include surface normal, optical vectors, intrinsic
color. We need more data to try our algorithms, especially with the emergence of
deep learning.

Computer graphics uses the same parameters to construct the world.

Blender is a computer graphic software, using OpenGL backend. Instead of spending
time to learn OpenGL, just to play with Computer Vision, Blender is a good start
because it's straightforward and quite intuitive

I am not going to show how do Blender, but when need will describe what the tool
is and how to use it.

I am not a professional blender designer, I am sharing what I found on my journey
to learn and understand computer vision.

